cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use benchprobe, cite this release by version and the study whose numbers you rely on."
title: "benchprobe: psychometrics for AI benchmark scores"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-11"
authors:
  - family-names: Zhu
    given-names: Louis Yiven
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5579-0340"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/louisyzhu/benchprobe"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for the psychometric analysis of AI benchmark scores: reliability and grader
  agreement (trust), factor structure and incremental validity (measure), leave-one-benchmark-out
  prediction with bootstrap uncertainty (predict), and continuous-response item-response scaling
  with anchor linking (irt). Every estimator is validated by reproducing the published numbers of
  three studies from hash-pinned data, with a per-number reproducibility ledger.
